# ── derived artifacts: everything here is regenerable, none of it is checked in ──

# The fetched 29 CFR 1926 corpus (~2.7 MB of federal regulation text).
# Regenerate: python fetch_osha.py --superseded
# It is pinned to a fixed eCFR snapshot date, so the rebuild is byte-identical
# on any machine, any day — which is exactly why it does not belong in git.
corpus/

# The Chroma vector index. Regenerate: python rag.py ingest
.chroma/

# Run traces — append-only, one file per working copy, no shared history value.
rag_traces.jsonl

# Secrets. .env.example is the checked-in template.
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# OS
.DS_Store
